  "description": "ENOXUB crystallizes in the tetragonal crystal system with space group I -4. Reported CIF formula moiety: C76 H144 Ce6 Mn4 N4 O44,4(H2 O1),4(C2 H3 N1). From the CIF bond table, Ce1 (Ce) has 8 O neighbors; Ce2 (Ce) has 8 O neighbors; Mn1 (Mn) has 5 O neighbors; Ce1B (Ce) has 8 O neighbors; Ce2B (Ce) has 8 O neighbors; Ce2A (Ce) has 8 O neighbors; Ce2C (Ce) has 8 O neighbors; Mn1B (Mn) has 5 O neighbors; Mn1C (Mn) has 5 O neighbors; Mn1A (Mn) has 5 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 24 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.214-3.893 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 86.26-128.28°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C76H144Ce6Mn4N4O44·4H2O·4MeCN. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 μ4-O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 4 μ3-O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 4 OAc (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)). Article name explicitly identifies Ce(IV), Mn(III).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
